    "post_canonical": "Let $ ABC$ be a triangle and $ AB\\ne AC$ . $ D$ is a point on $ BC$ such that $ BA \\equal{} BD$ and $ B$ is between $ C$ and $ D$ . Let $ I_{c}$ be center of the circle which touches $ AB$ and the extensions of $ AC$ and $ BC$ . $ CI_{c}$ intersect the circumcircle of $ ABC$ again at $ T$ . \r\nIf $ \\angle TDI_{c} \\equal{} \\frac {\\angle B \\plus{} \\angle C}{4}$ then find $ \\angle A$",
